  "findings": [
    "Construction starts from an edge, stores both endpoint node IDs, and extends an ordered chain at either end. It is not an unordered edge set or a free standalone-node tool.",
    "Candidate checks call _get_is_planar and _get_is_convex; closure calls can_add_plate before publishing the node loop and facing-side flag.",
    "Inner solid geometry adds the same normal-derived node support offset to each node. One active normal axis uses a face centre, two use an edge midpoint, and three use a cube corner.",
    "add_static_geometry computes a separate offset using G_VEHICLE_PLATE_THICKNESS, dispatches solid/window/opening/hatch inner geometry, and also calls add_geometry_outer. A single DoubleSide polygon is incomplete.",
    "Full outer strips, window frames, all placement blockers, runtime behaviour and same-camera screenshots remain unverified."
  ]
}
